  "summary": "Hutto City Council voted unanimously on Sept. 18 to discontinue the police department's use of 10 Flock Safety ALPR cameras, citing concerns that partner agencies accessing the data are not bound by HPD policies and questions about AI developments. The police chief said cameras were already turned off before the vote, and the article notes similar recent decisions by Pflugerville, Bastrop, Liberty Hill and Leander.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Hutto Police Department identified concerns that partner agencies accessing information from the system are not bound by HPD's own policies governing that data.",
      "paragraph_idx": 16
    },
    {
      "quote": "the city of Pflugerville voted not to renew its Flock contract, Bastrop ended its Flock contract, Liberty Hill removed its Flock cameras and Leander discontinued Flock services.",
      "paragraph_idx": 23
    }
  ],
